    "output": "Done. The scheduling engine is implemented and the full public suite passes.\n\n## What was implemented\n\nChanges were confined to `workgrid/scheduler/` (`engine.py` and `report.py`). The dependency and resource packages, `contracts.py`, and the package `__init__` surface were left untouched.\n\n**`workgrid/scheduler/engine.py` \u2014 `build_schedule`**\n\nFollows the documented per-task contract in a single pass over `topological_order(graph)`:\n\n1. **Order / graph integrity** \u2014 `topological_order` is called first, so `UnknownDependencyError` and `CycleDetectedError` propagate unchanged before any placement work happens.\n2. **Blocked dependencies** \u2014 if any dependency id is already unschedulable, the task is reported as `DEPENDENCY_UNSCHEDULABLE` with the sorted blocking ids in `detail`; its demand and window are not examined.\n3. **Impossible demand** \u2014 `constraints.validate_demand` is called and `DemandExceedsCapacityError` / `UnknownResourceError` are caught and mapped to `DEMAND_EXCEEDS_CAPACITY` / `UNKNOWN_RESOURCE`. These are classified, never propagated, so one impossible task does not invalidate the plan.\n4. **Placement** \u2014 `ready = max(end of scheduled deps, 0)`; from `earliest_start(ready, duration)` it takes the first candidate where `fits_at(...)` holds, otherwise advances via `earliest_start(candidate + 1, duration)`. Exhaustion yields `NO_AVAILABLE_WINDOW`. A small `_place` helper isolates this scan loop.\n5. **Report** \u2014 assembled through the existing `build_plan` so status, ordering, makespan and summary are derived canonically, with `peak_usage` from `constraints.peak_usage(placed)` and `summary[\"usable_slots\"]` from the calendar.\n\n**`workgrid/scheduler/report.py` \u2014 `render_plan`**\n\nRenders the plan only (no recomputation): header `plan <status> makespan=<n>`, one `%04d-%04d <id> <resources>` line per planned task in plan order (resources `-` when empty, otherwise `name=units` sorted and comma-joined), an optional `unschedulable a,b` line with sorted ids, and a single trailing newline.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- No rules were re-implemented: ordering, capacity checks, window math and peak usage all come from the existing APIs.\n- The engine writes only to local accumulated placements, leaving both rule packages and the immutable contracts unchanged.\n- Determinism comes for free from the topological order, sorted resource names and `build_plan`'s fixed `(start, task_id)` sort.\n\n## Verification\n\n`run_public_tests` (`python3 -B -m pytest -q tests`): **62 passed**, exit 0 \u2014 this covers the scheduler acceptance suite plus the pre-existing dependency and resource suites, including the shipped `samples/plan.json` end-to-end case (makespan 8, peak `{\"gpu\": 1, \"workers\": 2}`, `usable_slots` 8). Nothing was left unverified or outstanding; the hidden acceptance oracle was not available to me and is not claimed.",
